codex
The patch introduces a publicly triggerable Kakao summary cron endpoint and a repeatable reward exploit in the new check-in flow. These are functional/security issues that should be fixed before considering the change correct.

Full review comments:

- [P1] Require real auth for cron triggers — C:\Users\Hyun Jae Won\.antigravity\aftermind-checkmate\app\api\cron\kakao-daily-summary\route.ts:22-23
  When this endpoint is deployed publicly, any caller can set `x-vercel-cron-signature` to any value and bypass `CRON_SECRET`, because the code only checks that the header exists. For the new Kakao summary job this lets an unauthenticated attacker trigger messages to every opted-in user repeatedly and outside the intended schedule; verify the signature value or require the bearer secret for external requests.

- [P1] Prevent repeat rewards after deleting check-ins — C:\Users\Hyun Jae Won\.antigravity\aftermind-checkmate\app\(app)\checkin\actions.ts:74-88
  If a user deletes their check-in for the current hour, the `HourlyCheckin` row used to decide `isFirst` is removed while the +50 Emma ledger entry remains. The same user can then submit again in that hour, hit the `else` branch as a first check-in, and repeat delete/re-upload for unlimited rewards; keep a separate per-user/hour reward record or otherwise make the reward idempotent.
The patch introduces a publicly triggerable Kakao summary cron endpoint and a repeatable reward exploit in the new check-in flow. These are functional/security issues that should be fixed before considering the change correct.

Full review comments:

- [P1] Require real auth for cron triggers — C:\Users\Hyun Jae Won\.antigravity\aftermind-checkmate\app\api\cron\kakao-daily-summary\route.ts:22-23
  When this endpoint is deployed publicly, any caller can set `x-vercel-cron-signature` to any value and bypass `CRON_SECRET`, because the code only checks that the header exists. For the new Kakao summary job this lets an unauthenticated attacker trigger messages to every opted-in user repeatedly and outside the intended schedule; verify the signature value or require the bearer secret for external requests.

- [P1] Prevent repeat rewards after deleting check-ins — C:\Users\Hyun Jae Won\.antigravity\aftermind-checkmate\app\(app)\checkin\actions.ts:74-88
  If a user deletes their check-in for the current hour, the `HourlyCheckin` row used to decide `isFirst` is removed while the +50 Emma ledger entry remains. The same user can then submit again in that hour, hit the `else` branch as a first check-in, and repeat delete/re-upload for unlimited rewards; keep a separate per-user/hour reward record or otherwise make the reward idempotent.
